# Git commits

Never create a git commit. Do not run `git commit`, `git commit --amend`, or any other command that writes a commit.

The maintainer commits locally and wants that control. Do not offer to commit, and do not commit even if asked in chat.

Read-only git commands (`status`, `diff`, `log`) are fine when they help the task. Do not `git push` unless the user explicitly asks.
